&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;Odour &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;The proposed dormer window to
the rear of the proposal is located above the discharge of the kitchen
ventilation system serving the adjacent commercial property. Cooking smells may
well detrimentally affect the amenity of the future occupants of the flat. The
following condition is recommended:&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;





&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin-top:0cm&quot; type=&quot;disc&quot;&gt;
 &lt;li class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0cm;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;Prior
     to commencement of the development the applicant shall provide details of
     how they intend to minimise the effect of cooking smells on future
     occupiers. The details should be submitted to the Local Planning Authority
     ( LPA) for approval in writing.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
